---
title: Ads & sponsors
description: Every size of ad slot, the sponsor card, the affiliate product card — and the member gate that "remove ads" opens. Each one is labelled, each one can be closed, and none of them is a pixel size: they are ratios that shrink.
eyebrow: Component
source: src/components/ad.css · src/js/im-ads.js
---
<p>Three ways a site takes money, and one rule they share: <strong>say what they are</strong>. Every block on this page carries an <code>im-ad-label</code>. It is not decoration and it is not optional — a paid placement that looks like editorial is the fastest way to lose a reader for good, and in most places it is also the law. The label is part of the component so that removing it takes deliberate effort.</p>

<h2>The anatomy</h2>
{{#example style="max-width: 40rem"}}
<aside class="im-ad im-ad-leaderboard" aria-label="Advertisement">
	<p class="im-ad-label">Ad</p>
	<button class="im-ad-close" type="button" data-im-ad-close aria-label="Close this ad">{{> "icons/x"}}</button>
	<a class="im-ad-slot im-ad-empty" href="#the-anatomy">728 × 90</a>
	<button class="im-ad-remove" type="button" data-im-ad-remove="#ad-gate">{{> "icons/sparkles"}}Remove ads</button>
</aside>
{{/example}}
<div class="im-table-scroll">
<table>
	<thead><tr><th>Part</th><th></th></tr></thead>
	<tbody>
		<tr><td><code>im-ad</code></td><td>The block. An <code>&lt;aside&gt;</code> with an <code>aria-label</code>, so a screen reader can skip it. <code>im-ad-bare</code> drops the frame for a slot inside something that already has one.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-ad-label</code></td><td>The disclosure. Mono, small, never in the accent — it is a statement, not a badge to be looked at.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-ad-close</code></td><td>The cross, bare, in the corner. <code>im-ad-close-over</code> for a cross that sits on a picture.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-ad-slot</code></td><td>Where the creative goes. It holds the <strong>shape</strong>, so an empty slot and a full one are the same size and the page never jumps when one fails to load. <code>im-ad-empty</code> is the dashed "nothing sold this week" state.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-ad-remove</code></td><td>The way out. Quiet, at the foot; it opens the member gate.</td></tr>
	</tbody>
</table>
</div>

<h2>Every size</h2>
<p>The formats are <strong>ratios</strong>, not pixel sizes. A 728×90 leaderboard on a 390px phone is a 728px page with a sideways scrollbar; here it is a shape that shrinks, capped so it never eats the screen. Below 40rem a leaderboard becomes the mobile banner it should always have been — nothing in the markup changes.</p>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-grid-auto" style="--im-grid-min: 15rem; align-items: start">
	<aside class="im-ad im-ad-rectangle" aria-label="Advertisement"><p class="im-ad-label">Ad</p><button class="im-ad-close" type="button" data-im-ad-close aria-label="Close">{{> "icons/x"}}</button><span class="im-ad-slot im-ad-empty">300 × 250</span></aside>
	<aside class="im-ad im-ad-square" aria-label="Advertisement"><p class="im-ad-label">Ad</p><span class="im-ad-slot im-ad-empty">250 × 250</span></aside>
	<aside class="im-ad im-ad-banner" aria-label="Advertisement"><p class="im-ad-label">Ad</p><span class="im-ad-slot im-ad-empty">320 × 50</span></aside>
	<aside class="im-ad im-ad-skyscraper" aria-label="Advertisement"><p class="im-ad-label">Ad</p><span class="im-ad-slot im-ad-empty">160 × 600</span></aside>
	<aside class="im-ad im-ad-half" aria-label="Advertisement"><p class="im-ad-label">Ad</p><span class="im-ad-slot im-ad-empty">300 × 600</span></aside>
</div>
{{/example}}
<div class="im-table-scroll">
<table>
	<thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>Ratio</th><th>Capped at</th></tr></thead>
	<tbody>
		<tr><td><code>im-ad-leaderboard</code></td><td>728 × 90</td><td>48rem</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-ad-billboard</code></td><td>970 × 250</td><td>62rem</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-ad-banner</code></td><td>320 × 50</td><td>24rem</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-ad-rectangle</code></td><td>300 × 250</td><td>20rem</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-ad-square</code></td><td>1 : 1</td><td>18rem</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-ad-half</code></td><td>300 × 600</td><td>20rem</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-ad-skyscraper</code></td><td>160 × 600</td><td>11rem</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-ad-portrait</code></td><td>300 × 1050</td><td>20rem</td></tr>
